{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And behold, a ram.</b> It had been prepared for this since the six days of Creation." "<b>Behind.</b> After the angel said to him, \"Do not stretch out your hand,\" he saw it held fast — and that is how we render it: וּזְקַף אַבְרָהָם יַת עֵינוֹהִי בָּתַר אִלֵּין." "<b>In the thicket.</b> A tree." "<b>By its horns.</b> It had been running toward Abraham, and the satan entangled it and caught it in the trees." "<b>In place of his son.</b> Since it is written וַיַּעֲלֵהוּ לְעֹלָה, the verse lacks nothing — so what is תַּחַת בְּנוֹ? For every act of service he performed with it, he would pray and say: May it be Your will that this be as though it were done with my son — as though my son were slaughtered, as though his blood were sprinkled, as though he were flayed, as though he were offered up and reduced to ashes."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:58.426750785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}